body:
Research-backed adapter hardening pushed in `a7a5b24`:

- Gemini Live now traverses the same #95147 core/TUI provider path as OpenAI/xAI instead of falling back to the legacy runner;
- Gemini auth resolution is shared rather than duplicated in the CLI;
- provider readiness and recoverable failures survive neutral mapping;
- connected/listening waits for provider readiness;
- versioned/sequenced JSONL receipts include monotonic `session_ready_ms`, `endpoint_to_first_audio_ms`, and `interruption_to_local_silence_ms`;
- bounded capture/playback loss is counted and surfaced as rate-limited warnings.

Receipt: 124 focused tests passed; Ruff clean. The full SOTA audit and explicit remaining gaps (epoch/effect ledger, reconnect, semantic turn arbitration, surface-hosted transport) are on NousResearch/hermes-agent#77111.
